      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "9673b35d-7ab7-5053-8bde-0eee9a8197b4",
        ":question/problem": "$$\nf(t,z)=\u27e8\\text{_____},\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t,\\,z\u27e9\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,z)$ above parametrizes the elliptic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as ${x}^{2}+25{y}^{2}=25.$ What is the first component of $f?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that the ellipse \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+25{y}^{2}=25\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1\n$$\n\nin $xy$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n\u27e8x,y\u27e9=\u27e85\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\u27e9,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ),\n$$\n\nsince \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1} & =\\frac{(5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t)^{2}}{25}+(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)^{2} \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}\u2061t+{sin}^{2}\u2061t \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t,z) & =\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e85\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t,\\,z\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t.$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "9e118899-8a0e-5b48-82c5-20aecfe54e53",
